[[:db/retract 17592186162232 :question/answer-fields 17592186158934] {:db/id "q-110368/selection/ma-v1/e4360d86604650509214d31c7e692a4f6c261f986cd34dd7ce2d05eadfb977c6/99f48c1b72e8eeab33eba2584ff0661456642ba13c82a72d98a76e8e1a07563e" :answer/id #uuid "4cb70220-1466-50f4-a826-75372b44eff7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110368/selection/ma-v1/e4360d86604650509214d31c7e692a4f6c261f986cd34dd7ce2d05eadfb977c6/96ee6a3361e9d457b88fc124f1f022ef8dc27c2272728293b480cef1fc3f4e34" :answer/id #uuid "a289333e-2a6d-5f61-85e8-94509b25771a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{21}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110368/selection/ma-v1/e4360d86604650509214d31c7e692a4f6c261f986cd34dd7ce2d05eadfb977c6/0714d25b24bb2bd12cf1616a77c6da9f2b2196eee2490dd4d2f78efa4a0688c1" :answer/id #uuid "d8e2b385-ce1d-504d-ba33-f4bdb91683db" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4}{21}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110368/selection/ma-v1/e4360d86604650509214d31c7e692a4f6c261f986cd34dd7ce2d05eadfb977c6/17f7a92ecac965d3850a7da98658af322c6b691d4b3336f622586133c927298d" :answer/id #uuid "5664434d-a720-5066-af42-2f9c0df2a4e9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{11}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110368/selection/ma-v1/e4360d86604650509214d31c7e692a4f6c261f986cd34dd7ce2d05eadfb977c6/787ba90009a2104196393a6fa203fa7646fc82176685c8ab9f72d2176e83792a" :answer/id #uuid "4679fada-135d-51e7-be09-8da01fe5de7b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{21}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110368/selection/ma-v1/e4360d86604650509214d31c7e692a4f6c261f986cd34dd7ce2d05eadfb977c6" :answer-field/id #uuid "ed38c44f-3543-5960-9a58-1f8e5c55877e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-110368/selection/ma-v1/e4360d86604650509214d31c7e692a4f6c261f986cd34dd7ce2d05eadfb977c6/787ba90009a2104196393a6fa203fa7646fc82176685c8ab9f72d2176e83792a" :answer-field/choices ["q-110368/selection/ma-v1/e4360d86604650509214d31c7e692a4f6c261f986cd34dd7ce2d05eadfb977c6/99f48c1b72e8eeab33eba2584ff0661456642ba13c82a72d98a76e8e1a07563e" "q-110368/selection/ma-v1/e4360d86604650509214d31c7e692a4f6c261f986cd34dd7ce2d05eadfb977c6/96ee6a3361e9d457b88fc124f1f022ef8dc27c2272728293b480cef1fc3f4e34" "q-110368/selection/ma-v1/e4360d86604650509214d31c7e692a4f6c261f986cd34dd7ce2d05eadfb977c6/0714d25b24bb2bd12cf1616a77c6da9f2b2196eee2490dd4d2f78efa4a0688c1" "q-110368/selection/ma-v1/e4360d86604650509214d31c7e692a4f6c261f986cd34dd7ce2d05eadfb977c6/17f7a92ecac965d3850a7da98658af322c6b691d4b3336f622586133c927298d" "q-110368/selection/ma-v1/e4360d86604650509214d31c7e692a4f6c261f986cd34dd7ce2d05eadfb977c6/787ba90009a2104196393a6fa203fa7646fc82176685c8ab9f72d2176e83792a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-110368"] :question/problem "The random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)={\\begin{aligned}c{x}^{2}y,\\, & {x}^{2}\\le y<1, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nwhere $c$ is a positive real number. Find the value of $c.$" :question/worked-solution "To verify that $f(x,y)$ is a valid joint probability density function, we must check the following conditions:\n\n- $f(x,y)\\ge 0$ for all $(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}$\n\n- ${∬}_{{R}^{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y=1$\n\nFirst, let's sketch the region $D={(x,y)\\,:\\,{x}^{2}\\le y<1}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069972/assets/b9cfac7f0f82088900ab5e603588a73d4932f08f592321c797a1fd94b8bafb4e.png)\n\nNow, let's check our conditions:\n\n- Since $c>0,$ we clearly have $f(x,y)\\ge 0$ for all $(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}.$ So the first condition is satisfied.\n\n- For the second condition to be satisfied, we must have \n\n$$\n{∬}_{{R}^{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y={∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{1}c{x}^{2}y\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x=1.\n$$\n\nWe evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $y$, treating  $x$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{1}c{x}^{2}y\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{[c{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}]}_{y={x}^{2}}^{y=1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}c{x}^{2}(\\frac{1-{x}^{4}}{2})\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}c{x}^{2}(\\frac{1-{x}^{4}}{2})\\,\\text{d}x & ={[c(\\frac{{x}^{3}}{6}-\\frac{{x}^{7}}{14})]}_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{4c}{21}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\frac{4c}{21}=1\\,⇒\\,c=\\frac{21}{4}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-110368/selection/ma-v1/e4360d86604650509214d31c7e692a4f6c261f986cd34dd7ce2d05eadfb977c6"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-110370"] :question/problem "The random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)={\\begin{aligned}4xy,\\, & 0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind $P(X>\\frac{1}{2},Y>\\frac{1}{2}).$" :question/worked-solution "If $f(x,y)$ is a joint probability density function for the random variables $X$ and $Y$ and $A⊂{R}^{2},$ then\n\n$$\nP((X,Y)\\in A)={∬}_{A}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\nNotice that $f(x,y)$ is nonnegative in the region $D=[0,1]\\times [0,1],$ and the event $A={X>0.5,Y>0.5}$ corresponds to a subset of $D,$ shown as the shaded region below:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069972/assets/7e81ce16404bc6c5c826f79a88519bd6216156f5bb0f8af1eae41f19ca495de5.png)\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>\\frac{1}{2},Y>\\frac{1}{2}) & ={∬}_{A}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1/2}^{1}{\\int }_{1/2}^{1}4xy\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1/2}^{1}[{\\int }_{1/2}^{1}4xy\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1/2}^{1}{[2{x}^{2}y]}_{x=1/2}^{x=1}\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1/2}^{1}\\frac{3y}{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[\\frac{3{y}^{2}}{4}]}_{1/2}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{16}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-110856/selection/99f48c1b72e8eeab33eba2584ff0661456642ba13c82a72d98a76e8e1a07563e" :answer/id #uuid "520e3924-b343-5e89-9d38-37bdf3f71006" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110856/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer/id #uuid "5c8a22fc-162a-5a8b-8f79-d9fdcf239e9e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110856/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "dffded03-9e78-5f3f-b2ec-56927f538afd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110856/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "96bbebc5-eb79-55aa-b9a3-6b3a4cc371c9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110856/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "0b3e47df-84cc-5996-a9b9-d42b20841fe0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110856/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "20939478-94b3-5d13-a81c-6f5e5e62c267" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-110856/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer-field/choices ["q-110856/selection/99f48c1b72e8eeab33eba2584ff0661456642ba13c82a72d98a76e8e1a07563e" "q-110856/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" "q-110856/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-110856/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-110856/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-110856" :question/id #uuid "9f70ee20-c68c-558d-87a6-371d21272ed1" :question/math-academy-id "q-110856" :question/problem "The random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)={\\begin{aligned}c(x+y),\\, & 0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 1 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $c$ is a positive real number. Find the value of $c.$" :question/worked-solution "To verify that $f(x,y)$ is a valid joint probability density function, we must check the following conditions:\n\n- $f(x,y)\\ge 0$ for all $(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}$\n\n- ${∬}_{{R}^{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y=1$\n\nFirst, let's sketch the region $D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 1}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069972/assets/ea5ff670f03d0bffb84f0929d19b94bca62f23677f913c01e8e0949d144bc60a.png)\n\nNow, let's check our conditions:\n\n- Since $c>0,$ we clearly have $f(x,y)\\ge 0$ for all $(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}.$ So the first condition is satisfied.\n\n- For the second condition to be satisfied, we must have \n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}c(x+y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x=1.\n$$\n\nWe evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $y$, treating  $x$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{1}c(x+y)\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{[cxy+\\frac{c{y}^{2}}{2}]}_{y=0}^{y=1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(cx+\\frac{c}{2})\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(cx+\\frac{c}{2})\\,\\text{d}x & ={[\\frac{c{x}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{cx}{2}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{c}{2}+\\frac{c}{2} \\\\  & =c\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\nc=1.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-110856/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1a66952d-4e4b-5249-8f44-27d6fd198ea8"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-110856"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-110977/selection/7f28010b14e8ea81c315370fe04293ca974b7909014bdd06104bac532964d059" :answer/id #uuid "21aeb4dd-8dbb-51fb-9365-b307e26dbd2d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{e-{e}^{-1}+2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110977/selection/8b9f5d6b39487b08aa6b8017d21fd3b056d037d41aac199f5ede5da7d12244ec" :answer/id #uuid "a84b5601-20e0-57cd-a809-ec177f53504c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{e+{e}^{-1}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110977/selection/d577914c5b21ed2262816a93e2f03d38e892efed4543993c47f49fb12d630f7a" :answer/id #uuid "6c77e1fd-07ed-55a7-bd86-5191c4cd7665" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{e-{e}^{-1}-2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110977/selection/17c99e682018386edc5cd996e634ec7292efb102aedef894a3e984db89177c59" :answer/id #uuid "fb93a8b5-24f1-5ec0-a533-c519a5b92323" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{e+{e}^{-1}-2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110977/selection/fa4e5672862885455c9cd96bdc198df6c9bac97f438d060a686cf0a5e0bb914a" :answer/id #uuid "eec8dc82-7057-5421-9732-daacb7482412" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{e+{e}^{-1}+2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110977/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "13752dba-6066-53a9-8ce7-6c037e3fb26e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-110977/selection/17c99e682018386edc5cd996e634ec7292efb102aedef894a3e984db89177c59" :answer-field/choices ["q-110977/selection/7f28010b14e8ea81c315370fe04293ca974b7909014bdd06104bac532964d059" "q-110977/selection/8b9f5d6b39487b08aa6b8017d21fd3b056d037d41aac199f5ede5da7d12244ec" "q-110977/selection/d577914c5b21ed2262816a93e2f03d38e892efed4543993c47f49fb12d630f7a" "q-110977/selection/17c99e682018386edc5cd996e634ec7292efb102aedef894a3e984db89177c59" "q-110977/selection/fa4e5672862885455c9cd96bdc198df6c9bac97f438d060a686cf0a5e0bb914a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-110977" :question/id #uuid "6b0bdbbd-b393-5792-833a-168d560ed461" :question/math-academy-id "q-110977" :question/problem "The random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)={\\begin{aligned}c{e}^{x-y},\\, & 0\\le x<2y\\le 2, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $c$ is a positive real number. Find the value of $c.$" :question/worked-solution "To verify that $f(x,y)$ is a valid joint probability density function, we must check the following conditions:\n\n- $f(x,y)\\ge 0$ for all $(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}$\n\n- ${∬}_{{R}^{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y=1$\n\nFirst, let's sketch the region $D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x<2y\\le 2}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069972/assets/60acb4126a456e51e00db8bbeb2f8dbc6a773a4792dda7838d2aa6a3553fa739.png)\n\nNow, let's check our conditions:\n\n- Since $c>0,$ we clearly have $f(x,y)\\ge 0$ for all $(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}.$ So the first condition is satisfied.\n\n- For the second condition to be satisfied, we must have \n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2y}c{e}^{x-y}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y=1.\n$$\n\n$$\n{∬}_{{R}^{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y={∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2y}c{e}^{x-y}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y=1.\n$$\n\nWe evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating  $y$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2y}c{e}^{x-y}\\,dx\\,dy & =c{\\int }_{0}^{1}{e}^{-y}[{\\int }_{0}^{2y}{e}^{x}\\,dx]dy \\\\  & =c{\\int }_{0}^{1}{e}^{-y}[{e}^{x}]_{x=0}^{x=2y}\\,dy \\\\  & =c{\\int }_{0}^{1}{e}^{-y}({e}^{2y}-{e}^{0})dy \\\\  & =c{\\int }_{0}^{1}({e}^{y}-{e}^{-y})\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c{\\int }_{0}^{1}({e}^{y}-{e}^{-y})\\,dy & =c[{e}^{y}+{e}^{-y}]_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =c({e}^{1}+{e}^{-1})-({e}^{0}+{e}^{0}) \\\\  & =c(e+{e}^{-1}-2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\nc(e+{e}^{-1}-2)=1\\,⇒\\,c=\\frac{1}{e+{e}^{-1}-2}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-110977/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "129940fb-a409-55bc-9852-f68f4f9ffd11"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-110977"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-111162/selection/4e9d258b042599e2aad4fbd0e003f5c4785d79619ff4afc92dc14d3001b80161" :answer/id #uuid "fc542a1e-e22c-54de-81b5-237982ade082" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.827" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-111162/selection/40e42f8159bf7451216c10c22ef49435237cd51b912b5bfa4ff5f1f2b5078f89" :answer/id #uuid "3b36190b-4a87-5457-a180-2fb6f5b67c04" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.548" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-111162/selection/7c0b6891deddd9c032975b9cb4df5a88fd9ed86ec37bad429b929f54fc9a2449" :answer/id #uuid "d6187ac7-6872-5cc9-93d8-9f5b4ccc2ec6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.793" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-111162/selection/a0b83eeb50bd3cafc7ab0cde73ca1c777518c123ffddfb0b5b8c5e4da9eb5011" :answer/id #uuid "ac34920f-25af-5004-bc61-42d3e4b4330e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.613" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-111162/selection/f8d43007d089d4c6232cd8a0340cb760acf5e63753c689e78e97715cbec3c9c5" :answer/id #uuid "0567ab4c-a68a-53bf-b446-921d9d5cf6dd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.417" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-111162/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "cbf3b6e5-9a18-5a19-abfe-04aefac11ebb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-111162/selection/7c0b6891deddd9c032975b9cb4df5a88fd9ed86ec37bad429b929f54fc9a2449" :answer-field/choices ["q-111162/selection/4e9d258b042599e2aad4fbd0e003f5c4785d79619ff4afc92dc14d3001b80161" "q-111162/selection/40e42f8159bf7451216c10c22ef49435237cd51b912b5bfa4ff5f1f2b5078f89" "q-111162/selection/7c0b6891deddd9c032975b9cb4df5a88fd9ed86ec37bad429b929f54fc9a2449" "q-111162/selection/a0b83eeb50bd3cafc7ab0cde73ca1c777518c123ffddfb0b5b8c5e4da9eb5011" "q-111162/selection/f8d43007d089d4c6232cd8a0340cb760acf5e63753c689e78e97715cbec3c9c5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-111162" :question/id #uuid "5d73d54b-a64e-5f01-9abc-0112766b42d1" :question/math-academy-id "q-111162" :question/problem "The random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)={\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y),\\, & 0\\le x\\le y\\le \\frac{\\pi }{2}, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind $P(X\\le \\frac{\\pi }{4}).$ Round your answer to $3$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "If $f(x,y)$ is a joint probability density function for the random variables $X$ and $Y$ and $A⊂{R}^{2},$ then\n\n$$\nP((X,Y)\\in A)={∬}_{A}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\nNotice that $f(x,y)$ is nonnegative in the region $D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le x\\le \\frac{\\pi }{2}},$ and the event $A={X\\le \\frac{\\pi }{4}}$ corresponds to a subset of $D,$ shown as the shaded region below:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069972/assets/ea585fb6e12672f5cc854578cb12ff0357cfcd8d2f3d3b75a82723241cdaf3d4.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le \\frac{\\pi }{4}) & ={∬}_{A}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}{\\int }_{x}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y)\\,\\text{d}y\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}[{\\int }_{x}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y)\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}[-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+y)]_{y=x}^{y=\\pi /2}\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{2}))\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{2})]}_{0}^{\\pi /4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}-0+1 \\\\  & =\\frac{3-\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\  & ≈0.793.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-111162/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2bcf1eb2-cf04-5dd0-bb43-682c7e9cd953"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-111162"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
